/**
\defgroup FrameTransform_ext FrameTransform external: configurations involving external devices
\ingroup dev_tutorials

\tableofcontents

\section FrameTransform_intro Description
In order to integrate yarp own frame transforms management structure with other ones, like the one used by ROS/ROS2, new devices have been created to allow a bilateral communication between the two environments.\n
At the moment being the devices can be found in these two repositories:
- [yarp-devices-ros2](https://github.com/robotology/yarp-devices-ros2)
- [yarp-devices-ros](https://github.com/robotology-legacy/yarp-devices-ros) (N.B. this repository is not compatible with yarp versions > 3.10, but it is still available for legacy purposes)

The available devices are the following:
- frameTransformGet
    - FrameTransformGet_nwc_ros2
    - FrameTransformGet_nwc_ros
- frameTransformSet
    - FrameTransformSet_nwc_ros
    - FrameTransformSet_nwc_ros2
.

 In the sections below a brief description and simple graphic representation for each configuration are shown.\n\n

\warning To be able to use these configurations, if you haven't installed the repo built code, you have to add these paths to "$YARP_DATA_DIRS" environment variable:
- <path_to_yarp-devices-ros2>/share/yarp-devices-ros2
- <path_to_yarp-devices-ros>/share/yarp-devices-ros

.
 To see how different client and server configurations can be coupled, see the following page:
 \ref Fts_ftc_config_ext_config Fts_ftc_config_ext_config

\section FrameTransformClient

- **ROS ONLY** This configuration is to be chosen everytime a bilateral communication (publish and subscribe)
with ROS is needed.\n
The picture hereunder shows a simplified schema of the configuration.
Command line instructions to use the configuration:
\code{.unparsed}
yarpdev --device frameTransformClient --custom_config_context ros_frameTransform_config --custom_config_from ftc_ros.xml
\endcode
\zoomimage{FTC_ROS_Only.svg, FTC_ROS_Only}
  - **ROS PUB ONLY** and **ROS SUB ONLY** These two configurations have been added in order to allow
  a one way communication between the client and the ROS environment, be it publication or subscription.
  The picture hereunder shows, as in the previous case, a simplified schema of the configuration.
  To launch these configurations the following commands have to be used:
  \code{.unparsed}
  yarpdev --device frameTransformClient --custom_config_context ros_frameTransform_config --custom_config_from ftc_pub_ros.xml
  \endcode
  \code{.unparsed}
  yarpdev --device frameTransformClient --custom_config_context ros_frameTransform_config --custom_config_from ftc_sub_ros.xml
  \endcode
  \zoomimage{FTC_ROS_Pub_Only.svg, FTC_ROS_Pub_Only}
  \zoomimage{FTC_ROS_Sub_Only.svg, FTC_ROS_Sub_Only}
 *
  \subsection fts_sec_ros Client configurations that DO need a Server
The following configurations need, as the section title suggests, a running server component.
The appropriate client configuration depends on the running server.
- **YARP AND ROS** The last available version of the client uses both YARP and ROS.\n
It has to be used when a YARP only server is running and the client needs to store transform
coming from both YARP and ROS.\n
To launch this client the following command have to be employed:
\code{.unparsed}
yarpdev --device frameTransformClient --custom_config_context ros_frameTransform_config --custom_config_from ftc_full_ros.xml
\endcode
\zoomimage{FTC_YARP_+_ROS.svg, FTC_YARP_+_ROS}

- **ROS2 ONLY** This configuration is to be chosen everytime a bilateral communication (publish and subscribe)
with ROS is needed.\n
The picture hereunder shows a simplified schema of the configuration.
Command line instructions to use the configuration:
\code{.unparsed}
yarpdev --device frameTransformClient --custom_config_context ros2_frameTransform_config --custom_config_from ftc_ros2.xml
\endcode
\zoomimage{FTC_ROS2_Only.svg, FTC_ROS2_Only}
  - **ROS2 PUB ONLY** and **ROS2 SUB ONLY** These two configurations have been added in order to allow
  a one way communication between the client and the ROS2 environment, be it publication or subscription.
  The picture hereunder shows, as in the previous case, a simplified schema of the configuration.
  To launch these configurations the following commands have to be used:
  \code{.unparsed}
  yarpdev --device frameTransformClient --custom_config_context ros2_frameTransform_config --custom_config_from ftc_pub_ros2.xml
  \endcode
  \code{.unparsed}
  yarpdev --device frameTransformClient --custom_config_context ros2_frameTransform_config --custom_config_from ftc_sub_ros2.xml
  \endcode
  \zoomimage{FTC_ROS2_Pub_Only.svg, FTC_ROS2_Pub_Only}
  \zoomimage{FTC_ROS2_Sub_Only.svg, FTC_ROS2_Sub_Only}
 *
  \subsection fts_sec_ros2 Client configurations that DO need a Server
The following configurations need, as the section title suggests, a running server component.
The appropriate client configuration depends on the running server.
- **YARP AND ROS2** The last available version of the client uses both YARP and ROS2.\n
It has to be used when a YARP only server is running and the client needs to store transform
coming from both YARP and ROS2.\n
To launch this client the following command have to be employed:
\code{.unparsed}
yarpdev --device frameTransformClient --custom_config_context ros2_frameTransform_config --custom_config_from ftc_full_ros2.xml
\endcode
\zoomimage{FTC_YARP_+_ROS2.svg, FTC_YARP_+_ROS2}

.
\section FrameTransformServer

- The first one is the **YARP AND ROS** configuration.\n
 It starts a server listening to both thrift ports and ros topics, so its updates came from both parts. It has also a small storage inside to update
 all the clients that connects to it later with the latest transforms.\n
 the code to launch this server is:
 \code{.unparsed}
 yarpdev --device frameTransformServer --custom_config_context ros_frameTransform_config --custom_config_from fts_full_ros.xml
 \endcode
 \zoomimage{FTS_YARP_+_ROS.svg, FTS_YARP_+_ROS}

 - The second one is the **YARP AND ROS2** configuration.\n
 It starts a server listening to both thrift ports and ros topics, so its updates came from both parts. It has also a small storage inside to update
 all the clients that connects to it later with the latest transforms.\n
 the code to launch this server is:
 \code{.unparsed}
 yarpdev --device frameTransformServer --custom_config_context ros2_frameTransform_config --custom_config_from fts_full_ros2.xml
 \endcode
 \zoomimage{FTS_YARP_+_ROS2.svg, FTS_YARP_+_ROS2}
.
*/
